      "text": "### Algebraic Structure"
    },
    {
      "id": "14-COMPLEX-ANALYSIS.md#006",
      "path": [
        "14-COMPLEX-ANALYSIS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:mathematics:14-complex-analysis, git-history:mathematics:14-complex-analysis]",
        "canonical_path": "mathematics/14-COMPLEX-ANALYSIS.md",
        "concepts": "[complex, analysis]",
        "current_path": "mathematics/14-COMPLEX-ANALYSIS.md",
        "id": "maxim:mathematics:complex-analysis",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "mathematics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[complex, analysis]",
        "section": "mathematics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Complex Analysis - Complete Reference",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "ℂ = ℝ[i]/(i² + 1) — the ring of real polynomials modulo the relation i² = −1.\nEvery complex number: **z = x + iy**, x = Re(z), y = Im(z)."
    },
    {
      "id": "14-COMPLEX-ANALYSIS.md#007",
      "path": [
        "14-COMPLEX-ANALYSIS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:mathematics:14-complex-analysis, git-history:mathematics:14-complex-analysis]",
        "canonical_path": "mathematics/14-COMPLEX-ANALYSIS.md",
        "concepts": "[complex, analysis]",
        "current_path": "mathematics/14-COMPLEX-ANALYSIS.md",
        "id": "maxim:mathematics:complex-analysis",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "mathematics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[complex, analysis]",
        "section": "mathematics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Complex Analysis - Complete Reference",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "ℂ is algebraically closed (Fundamental Theorem of Algebra): every non-constant\npolynomial over ℂ has a root. ℝ is not — x² + 1 = 0 has none."
    },
    {
      "id": "14-COMPLEX-ANALYSIS.md#008",
      "path": [
        "14-COMPLEX-ANALYSIS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:mathematics:14-complex-analysis, git-history:mathematics:14-complex-analysis]",
        "canonical_path": "mathematics/14-COMPLEX-ANALYSIS.md",
        "concepts": "[complex, analysis]",
        "current_path": "mathematics/14-COMPLEX-ANALYSIS.md",
        "id": "maxim:mathematics:complex-analysis",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "mathematics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[complex, analysis]",
        "section": "mathematics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Complex Analysis - Complete Reference",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**Operations**:\n```\nz₁ + z₂ = (x₁+x₂) + i(y₁+y₂)\nz₁z₂   = (x₁x₂ − y₁y₂) + i(x₁y₂ + x₂y₁)\nz̄ = x − iy    (complex conjugate)\n|z|² = zz̄ = x² + y²\nz⁻¹ = z̄/|z|²  (for z ≠ 0)\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "14-COMPLEX-ANALYSIS.md#009",
      "path": [
        "14-COMPLEX-ANALYSIS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
